<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Varaguna II</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">9th century</span> · <a href="/centuries/9th-century">9th century</a> · Also known as Varagunavarman II</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Varaguna II was a king of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pandya-dynasty">Pandya dynasty</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/madurai">Madurai</a> in the second half of the 9th century. He continued the long wars of the Pandyas against the Pallavas for control of the Kaveri region, but around 885 he was defeated at Sripurambiyam by the Pallava king Aparajita and his Western Ganga ally. The defeat marked the end of Pandya ascendancy, and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chola-empire">Cholas</a> soon became the leading power of the south.</p></div>
